WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.740
I'm Jenna Fisher.

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.060
And I'm Angela Kinsey.

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.340
We were on The Office together.

4
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:08.580
And we're best friends.

5
00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:12.400
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.

6
00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:19.380
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.

7
00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:20.540
We're The Office ladies.

8
00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:25.340
Hi, everybody.

9
00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:26.900
Well, hello, hello.

10
00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:29.340
What is this energy?

11
00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:30.020
I don't know.

12
00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:32.280
I brought my roller skates today.

13
00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:34.600
Oh, this is roller skate energy.

14
00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:35.320
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

15
00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:36.900
You said you were going to do this.

16
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:38.760
I'm skating through The New Office.

17
00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.120
I want to show it to you guys.

18
00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:42.980
You might remember Angela skated through Earwolf.

19
00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:48.480
And when we came in here for a meeting, she noticed the floors were good for roller skating again.

20
00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:53.520
So like any 53-year-old, I brought my roller skates.

21
00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:55.360
And you're going to roller skate today.

22
00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:58.260
Just a middle-aged lady skating through her office.

23
00:00:58.400 --> 00:00:59.820
Well, this is what you're bringing today.

24
00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:00.500
And I like it.

25
00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:01.440
I'm here for it.

26
00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:02.240
Well, thank you.

27
00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:04.520
Guess what we're talking about today.

28
00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:06.220
Stairmageddon.

29
00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:11.580
It's season nine, episode 20, written by Dan Sterling and directed by Matt Sohn.

30
00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:17.360
Matt Sohn sent in some wonderful director's perspective audio clips on this.

31
00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:19.180
He's just the beSt.

32
00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:22.780
I know we've said this, but the other day I was at the grocery store and I ran into him.

33
00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:25.740
And I was getting takeout and I had all these bags.

34
00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:27.240
And Matt was like, Angela, what are you doing?

35
00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:30.920
And he walked across the parking lot, scooped up my bags, and walked me to my car.

36
00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:35.520
You know, we describe every person as the best, but it's because they are.

37
00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:36.160
I know.

38
00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:37.300
We were so fortunate.

39
00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:37.800
We were.

40
00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:38.820
All right, everyone.

41
00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:40.720
Here's your summary for Stairmageddon.

42
00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:43.180
The building's elevator is being repaired.

43
00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:45.300
And Stanley is not pleased.

44
00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:47.060
He refuses to use the stairs.

45
00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:48.240
It's a whole thing.

46
00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:48.880
Mm-hmm.

47
00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:54.400
Dwight has to use some unconventional tactics to force Stanley to join him on a sales call.

48
00:01:55.060 --> 00:02:00.160
And the first newspaper review of the documentary is published.

49
00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:07.080
This is going to lead to a lot of things, including Angela having to publicly defend Senator Lipton.

50
00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:14.720
Meanwhile, Toby and Nellie act as sort of sounding boards, surrogate therapists for Jim and Pam's relationship.

51
00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:18.400
Yeah, sort of relationship guides, these two, Nellie and Toby.

52
00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:19.200
Yeah.

53
00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:21.080
Interesting choice.

54
00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:21.500
Mm-hmm.

55
00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:23.560
And yet, worked out.

56
00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:25.820
Yet, like some real nuggets there.

57
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:26.200
Yeah.

58
00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:28.420
All right, everyone.

59
00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:33.400
For today's Top of Show, I'm going to kick things off with a fan question from Caitlin G.

60
00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:34.840
in Milton, Florida.

61
00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:39.600
Caitlin said, I have been waiting over four years to send this note.

62
00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:47.060
Stair-Mageddon is my favorite episode of The Office and possibly my favorite episode of television of all time.

63
00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:49.060
Caitlin, you love this one.

64
00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:49.800
Loves it.

65
00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:59.300
Caitlin says, the image of Stanley sliding down the stairs wearing that silly helmet and wrapped in bubble wrap makes me laugh to the point of tears every time I watch it.

66
00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:04.000
Every time I've had a bad day or needed a pick-me-up, I put on this episode.

67
00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:12.740
It has been a bright spot through my PPD, my husband's military deployments, and a cross-country move with two toddlers during the pandemic.

68
00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:14.180
Caitlin, my goodness.

69
00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:15.140
I know.

70
00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:22.640
Caitlin said, I truly can't explain what a gift this particular episode has been to my life and how excited I am to hear y'all break it down.

71
00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:25.280
You two and your team are a joy to listen to.

72
00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:28.900
Thanks for putting such a positive, cozy thing out into the world.

73
00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:36.920
Ah, well, I'm so glad that this episode has brought you so much joy, and I hope that our breakdown of it will bring you more joy.

74
00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:37.560
Same.

75
00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:40.520
I mean, Caitlin, you drove cross-country with two toddlers.

76
00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:41.340
I know.

77
00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:43.600
And to have your husband deployed?

78
00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:44.080
Yeah.

79
00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:45.600
That's a lot to hold.

80
00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:46.100
Yeah.

81
00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:53.020
We got another fan question about this episode from Kendall W in Phoenix, Arizona, who said,

82
00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:56.800
Please tell me Leslie David Baker will be a guest for this episode.

83
00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:58.440
I loved his storyline.

84
00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:03.620
Well, Kendall, I am very excited because I have been holding on to this for months.

85
00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:04.880
For months.

86
00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:05.560
Okay.

87
00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:10.680
So a while back, me and Leslie and Phyllis did a Cheerios commercial.

88
00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:11.780
We did a few.

89
00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:12.920
You're probably seeing them now.

90
00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:18.340
They were directed by Zach Woods, phenomenal director, and he's so smart and funny.

91
00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:22.280
But the four of us on set together, it was like old times.

92
00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:24.480
We were laughing so hard.

93
00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:27.980
I have all these pictures of us just cracking up between scenes.

94
00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:31.400
And we had lunch together on set, Jenna.

95
00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:32.220
Oh, my gosh.

96
00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:37.380
It was so crazy because you were doing like a mini office reunion commercial.

97
00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:41.980
And then I was doing a mini office reunion commercial at the same time.

98
00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:43.900
We were in two different cities, and it was so crazy.

99
00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:44.540
Yes.

100
00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:50.020
And Jenna, while you were doing your commercial, I was actually in St. Louis, which made me think

101
00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:52.640
of you even more because not only am I with the castmates.

102
00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:57.400
But anyway, we were at lunch one day, and it was me and Leslie and Phyllis.

103
00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:02.220
And I turned to Leslie, and I'm like, Leslie, we have got to hear from you on Office Ladies

104
00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:03.440
about your time on the office.

105
00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:05.120
And he was like, let's do it now.

106
00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:05.900
And I was like, right now?

107
00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:06.540
And I was like, okay.

108
00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:13.160
And I was like, I grabbed my phone, and he specifically talked about this episode.

109
00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:19.820
So here is my lunch break interview on my cell phone with Leslie David Baker.

110
00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:20.860
It is delightful.

111
00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:24.020
Hello, Office Ladies listeners.

112
00:05:24.020 --> 00:05:29.840
I am sitting here on the set of our new Cheerios commercial with Phyllis and Leslie.

113
00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:32.040
And Leslie's right here next to me.

114
00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:35.000
Hey, I'm here.

115
00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:36.160
Hi, how's everybody?

116
00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:41.860
Right now, Leslie's eating a really cute sugar cookie with a bumblebee on it.

117
00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:45.740
And we just had lunch.

118
00:05:46.060 --> 00:05:50.020
And Leslie, here are my Office Ladies questions for you.

119
00:05:50.180 --> 00:05:50.960
All right, shoot.

120
00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:53.460
How did you get your job on the office?

121
00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:56.060
I got my job on the office.

122
00:05:56.340 --> 00:06:01.640
Allison Jones called me in and said that she wanted me to audition for a show called The

123
00:06:01.640 --> 00:06:03.920
Office based upon the British version.

124
00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:07.520
I had never watched it, but heard it was successful.

125
00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:14.940
Went to the first audition, had on a very nice press shirt suit tie, was looking very elegant

126
00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:17.320
and dapper, did the audition.

127
00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:20.960
She told me, said, OK, I want you to go to the callback.

128
00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:24.880
But when you go to the callback, don't go in looking as crisp and pressed as you are.

129
00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:29.820
You want to come in looking kind of slumpy and kind of, you know, shirt wrinkled, disheveled,

130
00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:37.080
because you are at this paper company and you've been there for quite a time and you really don't want to be there.

131
00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:42.280
So I went to the audition, got to the callback audition.

132
00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:46.300
I had another audition that day for another project.

133
00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:51.260
And when I got to the office audition, there were about 50, 75 people there.

134
00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:52.360
It's a very crowded room.

135
00:06:53.060 --> 00:06:56.740
And I looked and I thought, so wait a minute, all these people are ahead of me.

136
00:06:56.920 --> 00:06:58.760
I have time to go to my other audition.

137
00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:01.880
Hopped in the car, left, went to the other audition.

138
00:07:02.260 --> 00:07:09.820
On the way back, ran into a lot of traffic and ambulances and school buses and every senior citizen in the free world out driving.

139
00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:17.080
So when I got back, I got to sit down and do my reading with Phyllis Smith.

140
00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:21.120
Allison Jones said, oh, Leslie, thank you so much for being patient and waiting.

141
00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:26.260
They said you were in the restroom, you know, and I would just went, oh, yeah, OK.

142
00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:28.220
No, my pleasure.

143
00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:29.980
I didn't mind waiting at all.

144
00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:32.420
And sat down, read with Phyllis.

145
00:07:32.920 --> 00:07:37.040
Greg Daniels told us, when you finish the scene on the paper, just keep going.

146
00:07:37.340 --> 00:07:38.900
He wanted us to do some improv.

147
00:07:38.900 --> 00:07:39.680
So I did.

148
00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:45.420
So I incorporated what I had just gone through driving through rush hour traffic with Phyllis.

149
00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:51.000
And Phyllis was feeding me all the, you know, good vibes that she was feeding me.

150
00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:52.620
And we bantered back and forth.

151
00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:59.600
And we looked up and the people at the casting table were laughing and, you know, cut me off and said, OK, thank you.

152
00:07:59.820 --> 00:08:00.800
And I went outside.

153
00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:02.580
Allison gave me two thumbs up.

154
00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:06.840
And I thought, you know, OK, she's just a sweet, loving, positive person.

155
00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:08.440
And I probably won't hear anything.

156
00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:10.460
A few weeks later, I got a call.

157
00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:14.020
And next thing I knew, they said, you booked it.

158
00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:19.180
So getting stuck in traffic kind of helped your audition.

159
00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:20.840
It helped a lot.

160
00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:31.400
And then after I booked it, then my agent announced to me that he was retiring from show business and turning his agency over to his best friend.

161
00:08:31.980 --> 00:08:34.080
And I went, oh, OK, no problem.

162
00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:43.120
And then while I was waiting to hear what happens with the office, the agency switched over to his best friend who had a heart attack and died.

163
00:08:43.140 --> 00:08:44.100
Oh, my gosh.

164
00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:49.620
A week later, I got a call from NBC saying that they were picking the show up.

165
00:08:49.780 --> 00:08:57.040
And then SAG called me and said that I didn't have to pay an agent 10 percent because there was no agent to pay.

166
00:08:57.300 --> 00:09:02.940
And we did, I think, six more episodes and then kept going.

167
00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:04.160
And voila.

168
00:09:04.700 --> 00:09:05.180
Wow.

169
00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:07.620
I never heard that story before.

170
00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:08.180
Mm hmm.

171
00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:10.020
OK, let's see.

172
00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:10.880
Next question.

173
00:09:11.220 --> 00:09:13.680
Do you have a favorite episode from your time on the show?

174
00:09:14.100 --> 00:09:21.520
Ah, the favorite one was, I think, when Dwight Rainn Wilson, you know, shoots me with the blow dart.

175
00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:32.760
And then he and Clark, they roll me up in bubble wrap and slide me down the stairs and roll me across the parking lot to go to a staff meeting.

176
00:09:33.060 --> 00:09:34.280
That was a fun one.

177
00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:37.640
That wasn't really me sliding down the stairs.

178
00:09:37.820 --> 00:09:40.360
They had this mannequin made.

179
00:09:40.360 --> 00:09:44.500
And I figured if I was going to look that bad dead, I probably would be cremated.

180
00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:48.160
But that was a fun episode.

181
00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:52.960
So if anybody ever offers to wrap you in bubble wrap and roll you across the pavement, let them.

182
00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:53.800
It's very comfortable.

183
00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:59.460
Oh, we had a fan ask, did you ever actually do a crossword?

184
00:09:59.460 --> 00:10:08.020
I started many, many crossword puzzles and everybody in the office would come by and scribble in my crossword puzzle book a few lines.

185
00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:17.040
I never got through a single solitary crossword puzzle book the entire nine year run because the paper gets flimsy after a while.

186
00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:23.240
So they replaced those books and then auctioned them, raffled them off, gave them a wave to charity.

187
00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:24.440
Do you have one?

188
00:10:24.580 --> 00:10:25.520
Were you able to keep one?

189
00:10:25.900 --> 00:10:27.820
I've got one.

190
00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:30.060
Yeah, well, one, I think one or two.

191
00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:38.420
But the whole concept of Stanley doing the crossword puzzle, I came up with that when Greg Daniels said, you're going into a staff meeting.

192
00:10:38.420 --> 00:10:44.260
What could you do in that meeting to show that you were in the meeting, but not at the meeting?

193
00:10:44.480 --> 00:10:54.160
And I looked around in the drawers of, you know, we had a bunch of stuff from the prop house and I came across this old crossword puzzle book and it was already filled out,

194
00:10:54.280 --> 00:10:55.680
but on camera it didn't matter.

195
00:10:55.900 --> 00:11:01.180
So I did that and I said, I'm going to deliver my line.

196
00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:03.220
And I had a couple of lines to Steve Carell.

197
00:11:03.400 --> 00:11:08.780
Instead of speaking directly to him, I just delivered the lines, but didn't look up for the crossword puzzle book.

198
00:11:08.960 --> 00:11:14.020
I figured if they didn't like it, you know, then, you know, I think Greg was directing that episode.

199
00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:17.280
I said, if he doesn't like that idea that he'll change it.

200
00:11:17.540 --> 00:11:18.340
He loved it.

201
00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:21.120
And Stanley and the crossword puzzle was born.

202
00:11:21.340 --> 00:11:22.300
I love that.

203
00:11:22.460 --> 00:11:22.980
I love it.

204
00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:23.360
Okay.

205
00:11:23.540 --> 00:11:24.380
Last question.

206
00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:27.680
When the show wrapped, did you take anything from the set?

207
00:11:27.900 --> 00:11:28.920
Oh my gosh.

208
00:11:28.920 --> 00:11:31.560
I have my original wedding band.

209
00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:35.360
I have my Thunder Mifflin thermos bottle.

210
00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:37.620
I've got some, a couple of mugs.

211
00:11:37.620 --> 00:11:42.640
I've got a couple of, some of the sports cars off of my desk.

212
00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:43.460
Oh, all your little cars?

213
00:11:43.500 --> 00:11:44.820
My little cars.

214
00:11:46.360 --> 00:11:52.740
I've got, I think, a name plate and some other little odds and ends.

215
00:11:53.260 --> 00:11:56.600
You know, didn't take the clothes because, you know, they're not.

216
00:11:57.560 --> 00:11:58.160
Yeah.

217
00:11:58.160 --> 00:12:00.220
I didn't take any clothes either.

218
00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:03.540
No, the clothes were not anything that I would wear in real life.

219
00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:06.660
But yeah, that was it.

220
00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:07.500
All right.

221
00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:09.020
Thank you so much, Leslie.

222
00:12:09.140 --> 00:12:09.640
You're welcome.

223
00:12:09.800 --> 00:12:11.080
Talking to me on our lunch break.

224
00:12:11.300 --> 00:12:11.820
You're welcome.

225
00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:12.320
Anytime.

226
00:12:13.660 --> 00:12:15.240
Angela, I loved it.

227
00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:16.480
I was so excited.

228
00:12:16.660 --> 00:12:19.600
You texted me and you said, Leslie said I can interview him right now.

229
00:12:19.820 --> 00:12:21.360
And I was like, do it, do it.

230
00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:22.580
I don't care that I'm not there.

231
00:12:22.740 --> 00:12:23.320
Just do it.

232
00:12:23.320 --> 00:12:25.760
And it was, I couldn't believe he brought up Stairmageddon.

233
00:12:26.020 --> 00:12:26.720
I know.

234
00:12:26.840 --> 00:12:28.120
Which we hadn't gotten to yet.

235
00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:29.040
And I was so excited.

236
00:12:29.360 --> 00:12:29.760
Yes.

237
00:12:29.880 --> 00:12:33.900
And I knew when we got to this episode, it would be the perfect time to play his interview.

238
00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:35.240
Oh, well.

239
00:12:35.240 --> 00:12:40.380
Well, I think now we've interviewed all of the main cast members.

240
00:12:41.080 --> 00:12:42.020
How fitting.

241
00:12:42.440 --> 00:12:43.760
I love that.

