1535
01:14:08.500 --> 01:14:10.900
Seems like there's a ton of red flags.

1536
01:14:11.180 --> 01:14:16.140
Can you ladies share your experiences with getting an agent and any similarities or differences

1537
01:14:16.140 --> 01:14:18.420
with Andy as he pursues stardom?

1538
01:14:18.620 --> 01:14:23.700
I just want to hear all about what you ladies think of Andy and his experiences with this agent

1539
01:14:23.700 --> 01:14:24.660
and starting out.

1540
01:14:24.920 --> 01:14:30.080
Well, obviously, you know, agents represent you to help you get jobs.

1541
01:14:30.280 --> 01:14:31.260
You don't pay them.

1542
01:14:31.520 --> 01:14:35.260
They get a percentage of your income if they book you the job.

1543
01:14:35.700 --> 01:14:36.220
Yes.

1544
01:14:36.380 --> 01:14:38.320
And that is a pretty standard amount.

1545
01:14:38.520 --> 01:14:39.380
It's 10%.

1546
01:14:39.380 --> 01:14:47.680
So if you ever meet with an agent who wants 25%, 35%, you're going to want to look elsewhere.

1547
01:14:48.100 --> 01:14:51.800
But the hustle after they get you the appointment is up to you.

1548
01:14:51.980 --> 01:14:53.000
You've got to do your homework.

1549
01:14:53.120 --> 01:14:54.000
You've got to learn your lines.

1550
01:14:54.120 --> 01:14:58.440
You've got to go in like a pro because ultimately, they might get you in the door, but you have

1551
01:14:58.440 --> 01:14:59.240
to get the job.

1552
01:14:59.500 --> 01:15:06.080
You know, when I was looking for an agent, I ran into a few kind of scammy situations

1553
01:15:06.080 --> 01:15:07.940
and I wrote about them in my book.

1554
01:15:07.940 --> 01:15:13.180
What I would do is I would send my headshot and resume out to different agencies, you

1555
01:15:13.180 --> 01:15:17.460
know, mostly small and medium-sized agencies since I was starting out.

1556
01:15:17.640 --> 01:15:19.320
And you hope to get called in.

1557
01:15:19.440 --> 01:15:25.340
And I got called into one place and they said, oh, we want to represent you.

1558
01:15:25.480 --> 01:15:28.340
But the first thing you're going to need to do is get new headshots.

1559
01:15:28.400 --> 01:15:30.860
And we recommend you use this photographer.

1560
01:15:31.440 --> 01:15:33.640
And it's the only photographer we used.

1561
01:15:33.640 --> 01:15:40.560
And I realized that really what this was, was just a way for them to make actors get

1562
01:15:40.560 --> 01:15:41.480
money photographs.

1563
01:15:42.340 --> 01:15:48.460
So it was like, they wouldn't represent you unless you got new photos and unless you used

1564
01:15:48.460 --> 01:15:49.520
their photographer.

1565
01:15:49.520 --> 01:15:53.460
And it was really just a photographer and a person who were kind of in cahoots.

1566
01:15:53.680 --> 01:15:53.920
Yeah.

1567
01:15:54.100 --> 01:15:55.160
Taking money from actors.

1568
01:15:55.540 --> 01:16:02.340
And then in another instance, I had a meeting with a, I'm putting these in quotes, agent who

1569
01:16:02.340 --> 01:16:08.000
presented me with a contract, which is not unusual, totally cool to sign a contract, but there

1570
01:16:08.000 --> 01:16:10.320
was a clause because, you know, I read it.

1571
01:16:10.420 --> 01:16:11.000
Good for you.

1572
01:16:11.200 --> 01:16:11.960
The whole thing.

1573
01:16:12.220 --> 01:16:18.280
There was a clause that said that there was like every year there was an option to renew

1574
01:16:18.280 --> 01:16:18.920
the contract.

1575
01:16:18.920 --> 01:16:22.700
It would automatically renew, but it was on their end only.

1576
01:16:22.700 --> 01:16:29.000
And so it could become like this never ending contract, which is also illegal.

1577
01:16:29.300 --> 01:16:35.600
And the cool thing is that the Screen Actors Guild has a department that will review agent

1578
01:16:35.600 --> 01:16:38.360
contracts for you and help you.

1579
01:16:38.580 --> 01:16:43.720
And so I sent that contract to one of those representatives at the Screen Actors Guild and

1580
01:16:43.720 --> 01:16:45.300
they said, no, no, no, no, no.

1581
01:16:45.820 --> 01:16:47.120
Do not sign that contract.

1582
01:16:47.520 --> 01:16:47.960
That's great.

1583
01:16:48.080 --> 01:16:48.820
I didn't know that.

1584
01:16:48.820 --> 01:16:52.780
Yeah, so they were awesome and they were a great resource.

1585
01:16:53.080 --> 01:16:59.640
But yeah, I mean, coming up, I had a lot of sketchy things that I had to kind of work

1586
01:16:59.640 --> 01:16:59.800
